{"slug":"lepidium-campestre","plant":{"taxon":"Lepidium campestre","family":"Brassicaceae","rank":"species","gbif_key":7703116,"wikidata":"Q149447","iucn":null,"gbif_occurrences":55866,"common_name":"field pepperwort","names":[{"source":"culpeper","name":"Mithridate Mustard","monograph_id":"cul:304-mithridate-mustard","confidence":"low","note":"Taller biennial, smaller round pouches, sharper taste; names applied to both species."}],"n_compounds":0,"top_compounds":[],"epmc_total":30,"trials":0,"claims":[{"concept_id":"abscess","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.88,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"amenorrhea","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.94,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"nausea_vomiting","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.84,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"poisoning","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.81,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"},{"concept_id":"sciatica","dsc":0,"cul":1,"persistent":false,"epmc_pair":0,"lift":0.94,"evidence_tier":"unstudied"}],"lead_score":null},"texts":{"cul:304-mithridate-mustard":{"ref":"Culpeper, Complete Herbal: Mithridate Mustard","headword":"Mithridate Mustard","lang":"en","source":"culpeper","text":"Both of them are herbs of Mars. The Mustards are said to purge the body both upwards and downwards, and procure women’s courses so abundantly, that it suffocates the birth. It breaks inward imposthumes, being taken inwardly; and used in clysters, helps the sciatica. The seed applied, doth the same. It is an especial ingredient in mithridate and treacle, being of itself an antidote resisting poison, venom and putrefaction. It is also available in many cases for which the common Mustard is used, but somewhat weaker.","spans":[{"start":57,"end":84,"concept_id":"nausea_vomiting","polarity":"action"},{"start":104,"end":127,"concept_id":"amenorrhea","polarity":"action"},{"start":151,"end":171,"concept_id":"abortifacient